we humans released more than 34 billion  tons of carbon dioxide into the  atmosphere in 2012 that's more than ever  before in spite of all warnings climate  change continues so what will happen if  we don't change  some experts predict that global  temperatures could rise as much as six  degrees Celsius by the end of the  century if those predictions come true  glaciers and polar ice caps will melt  and the sea level will rise entire  archipelagos and some land areas would  be flooded permanently not just the  rural areas would be affected cities  like London Tokyo and New York could end  up underwater the Earth's warming would  cause more water to evaporate resulting  in heavier rainfall and storms River  flooding would become a common  occurrence in some areas rising  temperatures would cause other already  arid regions to become even drier  resulting in more drought and desert  expansion in places like the Sahel  region in Africa  flooding or desertification and a  resulting shortage of food and clean  water would force many people to leave  their homes making them climate change  refugees countless animals and plant  species would be threatened with  extinction because they wouldn't be able  to adapt to the changing conditions  that's why the Intergovernmental Panel  on Climate Change wants to limit the  temperature increased 2 degrees Celsius  so the consequences are still manageable
 

